<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela bolivar softens to 474.25/475.25/dlr.</title>
<headline>Venezuela bolivar softens to 474.25/475.25/dlr.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Venezuelan bolivar softened to 474.25/475.25 per dollar as the Central Bank let the market meet strong demand for dollars, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The Central Bank didn't intervene,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>On Friday the unit closed at 473.75/474.75.</p>
<p>With yields on benchmark six-month Central Bank TEMs at an all year-low of 13.42 percent, traders said the bolivar could continue to weaken.</p>
<p>&quot;If these rates are maintained, the bolivar is going to suffer as more and more people buy dollars,&quot; said one trader.</p>
<p>-- Maria Jose Gonzalez, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600</p>
